      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This repeats the point instead of adding stronger support.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;B. Visual aids exist.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This is too general because it does not explain how the visual aid helps the audience.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;C. Visual aids are not connected to speeches.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This contradicts the point.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;D. A simple chart can show a pattern the audience might miss in spoken words alone.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Correct. This gives specific support and explanation.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q17</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.SPEECH.SPK.01&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which choice best supports audience understanding?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
