    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q24</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;A. Randomly speaking...&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This does not signal reasoning.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;B. This matters because...&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Correct. This phrase prepares the speaker to explain why support matters.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;C. On another topic...&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This signals a topic shift.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;D. Forget that point...&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;This does not explain support.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q25</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q25&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.SPEECH.COM.02&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which statement best summarizes this lesson?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>SPEECH_U02_L06_Quiz_Q25</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;A. Informative speech points need specific support, reasoning, and transitions that guide the audience.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Correct. This summarizes the lesson focus.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;B. Informative speech points should avoid support.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Support is necessary for clear explanation.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;C. Transitions should be random.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Transitions should show relationships.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;D. Reasoning should repeat the point only.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
      <feedback format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Reasoning should explain why support matters.&lt;/p&gt;</text></feedback>
    </answer>
